WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:15.354
SHOW ONLY THE OA LAYER
In the Explorer, ⊞ on OA scopes every diagram to the operational-analysis package. The chip above the canvas says what is shown.

2
00:00:15.354 --> 00:00:28.110
GENERAL VIEW
All of OA as boxes, read left to right: the people, drones and ground equipment of today's operation, and the activities allocated to each. No system is named.

3
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:41.572
READ ONE ELEMENT
Select a box: Properties shows what it is. memberA stands for one of the twelve drones, not an extra one. The purple lines on its left: the 14 activities it performs.

4
00:00:41.572 --> 00:00:53.628
TREE VIEW
What OA contains, one branch at a time. +N on a box opens what it owns: here the action definition HandOverSector and its two ports, one out and one in.

5
00:00:53.628 --> 00:01:06.546
INTERCONNECTION VIEW
The twelve kinds of entity and their fourteen usages: people, drones, ground station, radios, recharge and recovery points, cameras. No connections at OA.

6
00:01:06.546 --> 00:01:21.671
ACTION VIEW
The 38 activities, each allocated to the entity that performs it. No successions: at OA they are a set, not a sequence. The lines are the 33 flows between them, each labelled with what it carries.

7
00:01:21.672 --> 00:01:34.394
STATE VIEW
Four state machines: one drone's sortie and its operating condition, the fleet's mission and its mesh. Lines are transitions; most are labelled trigger / effect.

8
00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:48.051
READ ONE STATE MACHINE
A drone that loses satellite positioning goes from Nominal to NavigationDegraded and navigates by camera; when positioning is back it resumes satellite navigation.

9
00:01:48.051 --> 00:01:59.590
CASE VIEW
The mission, WatchTheTaskedArea, and ten capabilities as use cases. Each names its subject, holder: a drone, the duty controller or the analyst.

10
00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:12.389
REQUIREMENT VIEW
OA's hazards, each satisfied by an activity. Before recording we deleted one, ReportLostInLinkGapHazard, and its «satisfy» went with it. Now we add it back.

11
00:02:12.389 --> 00:02:21.981
SELECT WHERE IT GOES
A new element goes under the selection, so first select the Hazards package, inside OA, in the Explorer.

12
00:02:21.981 --> 00:02:32.112
PLACE A REQUIREMENT
Pick Requirement in the palette, then click empty canvas. The new requirement is created in Hazards and selected.

13
00:02:32.112 --> 00:02:40.128
NAME IT
Type its name in Properties.

14
00:02:40.128 --> 00:02:54.780
GIVE IT ITS TEXT
The statement goes in Requirement text, word for word as in the model: a report is sent into a link gap and nobody knows it never arrived.

15
00:02:54.780 --> 00:03:09.893
ITS «SATISFY» GOES IN GENERAL
acknowledgeReports, which satisfied it, left the Requirement view with it; General shows both. Select it and press Selection, then pick Satisfy and click it: the satisfier first.

16
00:03:09.893 --> 00:03:23.796
THEN CLICK THE REQUIREMENT
The strip above the canvas now asks for the target. Fit, zoom to the new hazard and click it: the «satisfy» is drawn, and filed in OA, where it was.

17
00:03:23.796 --> 00:03:39.857
THE RESULT
The Requirement view is as it was: four hazards, each satisfied by an activity. Not re-entered: the hazard's #Hazard tag, its subject and SA's «satisfy» of it. Edits stay in this browser until saved or exported.
